# One shell command per line, run from the repo root by githooks/pre-push.
# Non-zero exit refuses the push. Lines starting with # are ignored.
#
# This list is exactly what .github/workflows/ci.yml runs, and that is the whole
# point: a check that fails here fails in CI too, so you learn it in seconds
# rather than after a round trip. Adding a step to one and not the other is the
# defect - a local gate that runs a different graph from CI reports a verdict
# about a build nobody is shipping.
#
# Deliberately NOT here: a syntax check on tools/*.py. The tools are dev
# utilities that ship nothing; when story #11 exercises photos.py for real,
# revisit this.
#
# The linkcheck line below IS python, which the paragraph above used to say was
# impossible here: `python` and `python3` both resolved to the Windows Store
# alias stub, exiting 126. Measured 2026-09-03 on the owner's machine, all three
# of `python`, `python3` and `py` run a real 3.13.14 - the stub is gone. Do not
# read that as settled: cairn records this interpreter moving four times, each
# correction accurate when written and wrong within two days. `python3` is the
# spelling chosen because it is the one that works BOTH here and on the ubuntu
# runner, where `py` does not exist. If this line ever fails with 126 or "not
# found", that is the stub returning, not the check breaking.
#
# There is no build step. The sites are static files plus the one-line copy in
# the Cloudflare Pages config - see CLAUDE.md.
npm run --silent check
python3 tools/linkcheck.py hq
